{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed, etc., and they encamped in Sukkot.</b> It is difficult: did the verse not already say ״וַיִּסְעוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵרַעְמְסֵס״ and so forth, so there should have been no need to say anything other than ״וַיַּחֲנוּ בְּסֻכּוֹת״? It appears that the intent is to say that there was no other journey between Raamses and Sukkot, and this is why it joined ״וַיִּסְעוּ״ to ״וַיַּחֲנוּ״ — for otherwise, if it had begun with ״וַיַּחֲנוּ בְּסֻכּוֹת״ there would be no indication of this. And likewise, throughout all the journeys, Scripture was precise to join the encampment to the journey (Mekhilta, Exodus 12:37)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:17:04.697004362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}